## Observability

OpenTelemetry traces and metrics are wired in from day one. The service name comes from
`OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` (default: the repository slug); browser bundles cannot read the
environment, so vite/sveltekit use build-time `VITE_OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` and Angular uses
`environment.serviceName`.

Run `mise run otel` to start a local collector (Docker required). It installs a small,
system-wide Docker Compose stack shared by every project on the machine, so you only need to
start it once and every project you work on reuses the same collector. `mise` then sets
`OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` and the per-signal endpoint variables for you automatically —
nothing else to configure. Other tasks: `mise run otel:status` (is it up?), `mise run otel:logs`
(tail what the collector received), `mise run otel:down` (stop it). Collected data also lands as
newline-delimited JSON in the `forge-otel-data` Docker volume (`/data/traces.jsonl`,
`metrics.jsonl`, `logs.jsonl` inside the collector container).

Outside `mise` (for example a bare `go run`, an IDE run configuration, or a CI job that does not
shell through `mise`), nothing is exported unless you set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` yourself;
browser projects use `VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (Angular: `environment.ts`) instead.
